{"severity":"error","file":"errors/trusted_linear_reserved_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":5,"end_line":12,"end_col":8,"message":"`@[trusted_linear]` is reserved for the standard library.\nIts function bodies are trusted, not checked, to use each value once. To let a generic function accept a linear value, mark the parameter instead: `linear x : a`.","code":"trusted_linear_reserved","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/trusted_linear_reserved_1.march","start_line":14,"start_col":17,"end_line":14,"end_col":20,"message":"`S1` is linear, but `dup` is generic in a parameter of that type, so it may drop or duplicate the value.\nConsume the value here instead, or, if `dup` uses that parameter exactly once, mark it `linear` where `dup` is defined (`linear x : a`).","code":"linear_generic_param","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
